comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T06:51:28.004Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: list-all and --no-truncate now imply unbounded cost unless an explicit canonical budget overrides them; budget-compacted producer pages rebase next_cursor to the last retained item and disclose structured CLI/SDK/MCP recovery, preventing skipped hidden rows. MCP outputBudget now accepts the same unbounded escape hatch as CLI and SDK."
  "2026-08-14T07:55:44.180Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: top-level item producer pages now rebase a continuation cursor to the last retained row and disclose structured CLI/SDK/MCP recovery; list-all and --no-truncate returned 45/45 rows in a packed temporary project; linked tests and exact coverage pass. Residual acceptance remains for cursor-native continuation across every nested row-producing and assurance-verdict surface, so this item returns open."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T07:55:47.229Z","harness:codex",Budget compaction must rebase a producer cursor to the last row actually emitted. Returning the producer's original page-end cursor after dropping rows creates a silent data-loss gap even when has_more remains true.
